  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "text": "In a large soup kettle, wilt bacon over low heat until fat is rendered, about 5 minutes. Add butter and allow it to melt."
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Add onions and wilt over low heat for 10 minutes."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Add flour and cook, stirring, another 5 minutes."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "Add stock and potatoes. Continue cooking over medium low heat until potatoes are nearly tender."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Add corn, red pepper, and return the bacon; season. Cook 5 minutes."
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "text": "Add cream, cook 5 minutes more, stirring occasionally."
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "text": "Add scallions, adjust seasonings, serve immediately, garnished with cilantro or parsley."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "For spice: can add 1 small jalapeno, seeded and minced, 1 minute before serving or dash chili powder. Carrots instead of red peppers Turn it into a fish chowder by adding fresh or frozen cod or similar (if going this route, try substituting a small amount of clam juice for some of the chicken stock).",
